      blurb: "# $[objectname]\n\n*\"Beyond this veil lies my life's work; a compendium of reagents collected from the five corners of the world. A list hard won from beasts and botanists, of rock and river, in grave and grove. This compendium contains, to my current knowledge, every valuable form of reagent that one might gather to build the next generation of weapon, or brew the next staple potion. Use it wisely.\"* \n\n<br>\n\n<br>\n\n### @[](pfuakxdwta)\nMotes of elemental essence rising around primordial fonts. Arcane dust formed between clashes of eldritch storms. Mana crystalizing after great rituals complete. These reagents are often the most valuable, and most difficult to acquire, or to make. \n\n### @[](fxwhwqwcgm)\nThis category contains most reagents harvested from living creatures. Owing to the vast range of creature type that prowl the world, from elemental beings forged from stone, to the enchanted logs from a Treant, there may be overlap with the other reagent categories.\n\n### @[](mktnnbueuc)\nVines, fruits, mushrooms and trees, the flora of the world comes in *almost* countless shapes and sizes. These harvests forge the backbone of most alchemical creations.\n\n### @[](paxgbkwryj)\nWhether mined from the bowels of the earth, or instead harvested from a mountain's peak, the minerals of this world can serve as vital building blocks and alchemical catalysts. "
